## When to Involve Each Role in Decisions

### Product Manager Should Decide
- What to build (feature prioritization)
- Success metrics and acceptance criteria
- Trade-offs between features
- User experience and design direction

### Project Manager Should Decide
- Timeline and schedule
- Resource allocation and capacity
- Process and meeting cadence
- Communication and status reporting

### Technical Lead / Developers Should Decide
- How to build (architecture, technology)
- Code quality standards
- Testing and deployment approach
- Technical risks and mitigation

### Scrum Master Should Decide
- Sprint length and iteration cadence
- Ceremony timing and facilitation approach
- Process improvements and retrospective topics

### QA/Testing Should Decide
- Test strategy and test coverage
- Acceptance criteria testability
- Release readiness criteria
- Quality metrics and thresholds

### DevOps Should Decide
- Infrastructure and deployment approach
- Monitoring and alerting strategy
- Rollback procedures
- Deployment windows and schedules

